Yep, Slash'em can give you a few more challenge for some time.
Then, you can also try to apply some patches (to either Nethack or  
Slash'em). The (full) Lethe patch is a good one to have more stuff to do  
in the late game...

Personally, it took me approx 12 months to ascend in Nethack (monk), then  
I switched to Slash'em and needed 3 more months to ascend (monk again). I  
still have not ascended Slash'em + Lethe even if I had a quite good game  
that died of carelessness.

Another good thing to do to get more interest is to write patchs... If you  
at least basic skill in C and algorithms, you can probably give it a try  
(starting with small stuff and then trying for bigger).


On a completely different matter, Battle for Wesnoth (a turn based  
strategy game) is also quite challenging and addictive (actually, I've  
almost stopped playing Slash'em on regular basis last year because of  
Wesnoth).
